  "digital_notes": [
    "U+06DC serves two unrelated functions: seen above a sad (2 places, alternative letter reading) and the saktah marker (5 places). Classification requires inspecting the base character.",
    "Tanwin shape is not in the encoding. U+064B/064C/064D each cover both the stacked and the staggered arrangement, so a codepoint-level diff will call two texts identical while one prints the wrong tajwid ruling. Unicode's U+08F0-U+08F2 open forms exist for the distinction but are unused by mainstream Uthmani corpora — normalising between the two conventions destroys it. Test by rendering, not by string comparison.",
    "Unicode names can contradict the printed form. U+06EA is named 'Empty Centre Low Stop' but the appendix specifies a filled dot (نقطة كبيرة مطموسة) and that is how it prints.",
    "The widely circulated Tanzil 'uthmani' text contains zero U+06D6-U+06DB characters — the waqf signs are stripped. Verify a corpus before building pause-aware features on it.",
    "The sajdah has two anchors. In 4 of 15 cases the overline and the mihrab glyph sit on different verses, up to two lines apart."
  ],
